[quote="MindWanderer"]

True, but honestly, I think the whole Overcome table is broken.&nbsp; If you can&#39;t use a Principle on the roll, even attempting an Overcome should be an act of desparation, i.e. the stakes are so high that it&#39;s worth a heavy cost to pass it right now.&nbsp; From Dave&#39;s comments, I infer that it was balanced with Principles in mind.

[/quote]

&nbsp;

first of all, thanks for the source of where you got your information from. &nbsp;I appreciate it.

&nbsp;

secondly, remember that damage is the most boring minor twist of the bunch. &nbsp;Look at all of the other twists we came up with that aren&rsquo;t that bad. &nbsp;A minor persistent hinderance that anyone can overcome, maybe just angering/annoying another player (such as Stella Nova painfully pulling memories out.) &nbsp;Or activating a curse that you were trying to avoid. &nbsp;(Like stella nova teleporting the talisman but not the box at the end of ep. 2).&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Minor twists aren&rsquo;t nessissarily all that bad. &nbsp;That&rsquo;s why I think they should do less damage. &nbsp;A minor twist shouldn&rsquo;t take you from yellow health to out.
